# Push updates when done

When you finish a task that changes the codebase (especially `nextgrades-app/`), **always push to `main`** before considering the work complete. Do not wait for the user to ask.

## Workflow

1. Verify the change builds if you touched app code (`npm run build` in `nextgrades-app/` when not already verified).
2. Stage and commit with a concise message describing the **why**.
3. Run `git push origin main`.
4. If About/marketing images were updated, run `node scripts/sync-marketing-cms-images.mjs` in `nextgrades-app/` when CMS overrides may still point at old assets.
5. Report push status in the final message (commit hash or note if nothing to push).

## Scope

- Push after substantive app/UI/locale/API changes.
- Skip commit/push for docs-only or local-only assets **unless** the user asked for those changes to go live.
- Never force-push to `main`.

## Deploy

After pushing app changes, follow the Vercel deploy rule: Git integration should deploy; mention that the user may need a hard refresh (Ctrl+Shift+R) after deploy.
